@ November 11, 2026

Hey there,

The 26.7 series gets another installment with a few nice feature addition
and UX revamps.  There are 4 new security advisories on GitHub for the
core as well as numerous fixes throughout the components as they are being
reported.  Of special note is that this update brings a number of performance
improvements throughout the system.

We have added "authority" annotations for the privilege selection and user
overview.  They aim to explain how much access to the system is granted to
the user in principle: the default is "administrative" as even though single
privilges appear to be low priviliges they are not as administrative (root)
tasks are being carried out by the underlying daemons and software.  The
"limited" label means the user does not have access to root processes and
the "unrestricted" label means that the component being accesses has no
bounds to system access which may be part of its intended feature scope
such as XMLRPC access.  We have also marked the static PHP pages as
"unrestricted", because in reality they have historical privilege separation
weaknesses that the MVC do not have.  This approach will also help shape
how we accept security advisories and set their severity.

